\b MIRA / THE LAST NIGHT\b0\par
24 October 1996\par\par
To the person who opens this disk,\par\par
The station closes at dawn. We have boxed the plates, disconnected the telephone, and covered the west lens. The north lamp still lights itself at 03:17. It is no longer connected to the clock.\par\par
I saved one image before the generator stopped. The arc above the dome is not a scratch. Compare the final entry in STARLOG with the terminal log. Seventeen pulses. No catalog name.\par\par
If you hear the relay, do not answer it. Leave the image open until morning. Someone should see what we saw.\par\par
M. Vale\par
Station archivist\par\par
\i FICTIONAL DEMONSTRATION. All people, places and events are invented.\i0\par
